      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T11:08:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually we should remove this restriction. The application can use `Load` \u0026 `Clear` loadOp with `RenderPassDescriptorResolveRect`, in that case that rect will only be used for resolve step, and will be ignored in the loading step.\n\nIt\u0027s valid for the application to do something like this:\n- Create a render pass with MSAA texture size 3x3, resolve target 5x5\n- Clear the entire MSAA texture. (loadOp\u003dClear).\n- Draw some stuffs to the MSAA texture.\n- Resolve MSAA (1, 1, 2, 2) region to the resolve texture\u0027s (3, 3, 2, 2).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 879,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 879,
